val=("ROUND 2 (replaces round 1; joint N+S fit with beam overlap, two-sided T_b, finer extended grid, tau<=3, free filling, LOO, bootstrap, dust cap). "
"(1) Model: compact C at each nucleus (Gaussian FWHM theta 0.15-1.2\", clump filling f_C 0.1-1, Tk 10-300, log n 3.5-7.5, N(HCO+) 1e13-3e17, A=N(HCN)/N(HCO+) 0.3-10) + ONE shared extended E (Tk 10-316 step 0.075 dex, log n 3.5-6 step 0.125, N(HCO+) 3e12-3e15, A, f_E 0.1-1, tau<=3), dv=150 km/s shared. N-S separation 5.2\" (PA~178): the 10\" beam (FWHM 10\") centred on one nucleus sees the other nucleus's compact core with weight exp(-4ln2 (5.2/sqrt(theta^2+100))^2)~0.48; converged offsets (S core in N 10\" ladder) are 0.1-0.7 K km/s vs 10\" fluxes of ~10-40 (<5%), added as a fixed term with 30% error; E is common to both beams (it is the shared gas). 28 data (12+2 per nucleus: 10\" ladders, 2.2\" 1-0/3-2, 1.29\" 3-2 T_b, 0.24\" 3-2 peak T_b as TWO-SIDED data with 15% error). "
"(2) Fit quality: joint min chi2 24.9 (N 17.1, S 7.8; 28 data, ~17 nominal parameters, grid-limited, dof ~11): one-state-two-size min chi2 51.6 (N), 40.0 (S). Parametric bootstrap (24 sims/nucleus, errors as assumed): if the one-state model is true, chi2(1s)-chi2(2p) never exceeds 10.4 (N), 10.8 (S) vs observed 34.5/34.3 (p<0.04 each, 24 sims); if the two-phase model is true the expected chi2_2p is 9.0 [3.9,15.4] (N), 8.8 [4.0,15.0] (S): the N fit (17.1) is mildly poor (p~0.04-0.08), S fine (p 0.75-0.92); the S Dchi2 of 34 is typical for a two-phase truth (p=0.17 that the sim exceeds it) i.e. S is consistent with either truth; the preference for two phases is real but driven by the data ensemble, not by one point. ln Bayes factor (shared-E two-phase / product of one-state-two-size) = 29.5 (base); LOO/variants: tau<=1 28.8, errors 15/20/20/25% 12.5, drop 2.2\" 1-0 33.2, drop 1.29\" 18.3, drop 0.24\" T_b 8.7, drop all 2.2\" 27.7, drop all 10\" data 7.8; always >7 (absolute values depend on the error model and the Occam volume). Shared E vs separate E for N and S: ln Z -40.65 vs -47.59 (ln BF 6.9 for shared; the N-S extended gas is consistent with the same state, as expected at 5.2\" separation). "
"(3) Extended phase (shared; profile likelihood, marginalised over the rest and both compact phases): Tk_E best 133 K, dchi2<4 for 79-133 K, excluded (dchi2>4) below 79 K (chi2 rises 0.3 at 79, 5.9 at 67, 10.4 at 56, 16.9 at 40 K, and 7.7 at 158, 15.6 at 224 K); log n_E best 4.0 (3.62-4.75 at dchi2<4; n_E 4e3-6e4, P(n_E<1e5)=0.99); N(HCO+)_E 1e14 (6e13-1.6e14), A_E 3 (grid edge-limited, 0.5 in log), f_E 0.3-1. Tk-n degeneracy: at fixed log n_E=4.0 the minimum is at 79 K (chi2(Tk) 0.3 at 79 K, 18.8 at 112 K, 48 at 40 K), at 4.5 at 79-112 K (7-8), at 5.0 at 112 K (6.4), and at log n_E=5.5 the best is 56 K at dchi2 19: the allowed region is a narrow ridge Tk~80-130 K with n 1e4-5e4, not a free degeneracy. P(Tk_E>50)=1.00 in base/tau1; LOO: dropping 2.2\" 1-0 or all 2.2\": Tk_E 40-112 K / 47-112 K; dropping the 0.24\" pair 67-133; larger errors 67-188; dropping all 10\" data: unconstrained (10-188 K). So the warm extended phase needs the 10\" ladder (J=2-1..4-3), and Tk_E>~40 K holds in every variant that includes it. "
"(4) Compact phases (two-sided 0.24\" T_b): size FWHM 0.5\" (~100 pc; grid 0.3-0.8\") for both nuclei (theta<=0.3\" excluded, P=0.00), f_C=1 (N; P(f_C<1)=0.30) and 0.3 (S; P(f_C<1)=0.86), N(HCO+)_C 3e15-1e16, log n_C 6.5 [5,7] (N), 6 [5,6.5] (S), A_C 3 [1-3] (N) vs 1 [0.3-3] (S), i.e. the N/S HCN excess is again in the compact phase (N/S ratio of A_C ~3, the 1-sigma ranges overlap). Tk_C is bimodal and data-limited: P(Tk_C<=30 K)=0.68 (N), 0.49 (S) vs prior 0.30; P(30-100 K)=0.04/0.39; P(>100 K)=0.28/0.12. The cold preference at N is driven by the 2.2\" data: drop 2.2\" 1-0 -> P(cold)=0.23, drop all 2.2\" -> 0.29 (=prior), drop 0.24\" T_b -> 0.39, drop 1.29\" -> 0.55, larger errors 0.58, tau<=1 0.70. So Tk_C remains unconstrained at N at the level of the systematic budget; S is mid-range 16-160 K. "
"(5) Two-sided 0.24\" T_b: best cold N solution (Tk 10 K, n 1e7, N 3e15, theta 0.5\", f_C 1) predicts 0.24\" T_b(HCN/HCO+) = 2.87/3.85 K (observed 2.65/2.75; HCO+ over-predicted 40%, chi2(0.24\" pair)=7.4); best warm N solution (251 K, f_C 0.3) 2.62/3.61 (chi2 4.4); S cold 1.22/2.48 (obs 1.18/2.81), S mid 1.08/2.57, S warm 0.97/2.67. The two-sided data remove 300 K f_C=1 solutions (they overshoot by >1.5x) but are met by f_C 0.3 + 250-300 K (clumping), so the floor/ceiling only breaks the Tk-f_C degeneracy partly. "
"(6) Testable predictions (N, branch best fits / posterior-weighted medians; S similar): cold (Tk_C<=30 K): HCN 3-2/1-0 T_b at 0.5\" 0.61, HCN 4-3 T_b(0.5\") 0.65 K, 4-3/3-2 0.34, H13CN/HCN 4-3 in 2.7\" 0.06 (X=50); mid (100 K, n 1e5): 0.35, 0.44 K, 0.35, 0.04; warm (>100 K): 0.63, 0.98 K, 0.60, 0.10 (limit 0.12 3sigma). DECISIVE: HCN 4-3/3-2 at <=0.5\" (0.34 vs 0.60) and the 4-3 peak T_b (0.65 vs 0.98 K); the 3-2/1-0 ratio does not separate cold from warm (0.61 vs 0.63); H13CN 4-3 only marginally (warm near the limit 0.12); HCN v2=1: collisional population exp(-1050 K/Tk) <= 0.02 even at 300 K, so the existing limits (v2=1f/v0<0.02-0.03) do NOT discriminate the Tk_C branches (they test IR pumping only). Compact gas mass (100 pc, theta 0.5\"): cold N 8e8/3e8/8e7 Msun at X(HCO+)=1e-9/3e-9/1e-8 (n_H2 3e6, n x size 3e8 cm-3 pc); warm 2.5e8/8e7/2.5e7 (n 1e5, n x size 1e7); S cold 8e8/3e8/8e7. The cold branch at X<3e-9 gives Sigma_compact ~(2-7)e4 Msun/pc2 in 100 pc, a mass comparable to or above plausible dynamical masses, which favours X>=3e-9 or the warm branch (not tested against the 0.24\" continuum here). "
"(7) Dust tension (extended column capped by Sigma(10\")<=77 Msun/pc2, Td>=30 K; hard cap on f_E N(HCO+)_E, compact capped too): X(HCO+)=1e-8: joint chi2 26.6 (vs 24.9 uncapped; dchi2 1.7: ladder still fits), Tk_E 79-133 K, log n_E 4.4-5.1, ln BF vs one-state 27.7; X=3e-9: chi2 33.9 (dchi2 9.0; Tk_E 67-112, log n_E 5.0-5.1: shifts to denser/cooler E); X=1e-9: chi2 104.6 (dchi2 80, REJECTED; the fit collapses to log n_E 5.9 and Tk_E 33-56 K, ln BF vs one-state -13.7); with the stricter Sigma<=14 (Td 100 K): X=1e-8 chi2 60.7 (dchi2 36, rejected), X=1e-9 rejected (chi2 486). POSITION: the two-phase ladder with an extended optically thin column is consistent with the continuum bound only for X(HCO+)>=~5e-9-1e-8 and Td<~30-50 K; X(HCO+)<=3e-9 or Td>~60 K contradict it, so either X(HCO+) is at the top of the usual range in this merger or the extended phase has lower column/higher filling structure than a uniform LVG slab. X(HCO+) cannot be measured here (no matched 10\" H13CO+). With the cap the extended Tk>50 and the ridge stay (Tk_E>=67 K at X>=3e-9). "
"(8) Verdict: the 10\" ladders, 2.2\"/1.29\" fluxes, 0.24\" T_b (two-sided) and H13CN limit are fitted (chi2 24.9/28 data) by a warm (80-130 K), moderately dense (1e4-5e4), thin extended gas shared by N and S plus a ~100 pc thick compact phase at each nucleus; the N HCN excess lives in the compact phase; Tk_C (cold vs >100 K) is not decided by existing data and the compact size is 0.5\" (grid-limited).")
